// destroyers with them; Togo's battle divisions come out of the haze to the north-east, crossing ahead to cap the
// Russian line. The forces are history's, thinned; the classes are stand-ins (Designs/: oslyabya also stands for
// Sissoi Veliky and Navarin, izumo for Kasuga, Nisshin and the armoured cruisers, aurora for Oleg), set for balance
// rather than tonnage:
//   Japan, the hunters: faster (an 18 kn line and 21 kn armoured cruisers), many 6 and 8 in quick-firers, trained
//   crews, 29 kn destroyers with two tubes; the armoured cruisers' belts are thin and their main guns light.
//   Russia, the hammer: more heavy guns (twelve 12 in and twelve 10 in against sixteen 12 in and twenty-four 8 in),
//   the Borodinos' 6 in in turrets, heavier armour; but an old second division that makes 16 kn, average crews,
//   26 kn destroyers (with three tubes).
// The weather of the day: haze, about 7 miles' sight, a fresh south-westerly.
